\subtree{
\title{2.3 The arena's own procedure on the merged build}

\p{As in [the run on the release](rep-AR2): the arena's complete test set (148 good tests with the eight corpora among them, 92 bad, 30 either), the run line of \src{scripts/arena/rlvm.yaml} as it stands with no option beyond it (8 worker threads), one container with the arena's limits (8 performance cores, 16 GB, no network), the tests one after the other with the arena's time limit per test, instruction counters and GNU time around the run line, the whole suite inside one quiet window. Once through the development executable (09:41 to 09:43 UTC, 87 s) and once through the release-layout executable (09:43 to 09:44 UTC, 88 s), then four single Mathlib runs, two per executable, each in a container of its own (09:44 to 09:45 UTC). The other cores of the host were idle.}

\table{
\tr{\th{executable}\th{good: accepted / rejected / declined / error / timeout}\th{bad: rejected / accepted / declined}\th{either: accepted / rejected / declined}\th{wrong accepts}\th{wrong rejects}}
\tr{\td{development (sha256 \code{3b4dfc34d447})}\td{148 / 0 / 0 / 0 / 0}\td{92 / 0 / 0}\td{11 / 17 / 2}\td{0}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{release layout (sha256 \code{b8c74c893326})}\td{148 / 0 / 0 / 0 / 0}\td{92 / 0 / 0}\td{11 / 17 / 2}\td{0}\td{0}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{No wrong accept, no wrong reject, no error, no timeout}, on both executables. The two agree in status and exit code on all 270 tests, and both agree on all 270 with the run of the release (rep-AR2, development image).}
\li{\strong{Declined, both executables:} \code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-no-whnf~} and \code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-and-no-whnf~}, both of the class either, the pair on which the official kernel does not terminate; 1.80 s and 53.55 G instructions each, against a limit of 60 s. The either tests split 11 accepted, 17 rejected, 2 declined, as on the release.}
\li{Instruction counts of the two executables agree within 0.5 percent on every one of the 30 tests above 1 G (the largest difference: \code{\verb~|perf/unfold-before-literal-bad~}, 0.48 percent).}
\li{The largest share of a time limit is 4.5 percent, \code{\verb~|perf/proj-applied-struct-arg-bad~} with 5.4 s of 120 s. The largest resident set of a small test is 2,369 MiB (\code{\verb~|perf/gf3-matrix-product~}), of the suite 3,689 MiB (Mathlib).}
}

