\subtree{
\title{4. The benchmark rows of the merged build, and the optional build}

\p{The rows of [the benchmark tables](rep-benchmarks) were taken again for the merged build, in ten quiet windows between 10:20 and 10:39 UTC with the other cores idle (fewer than 0.15 CPUs of the host busy before every window): the executable in its default configuration, the JVM launcher, the reference engine by name on the executable, the instruction counts of a cold process in the arena-shaped container for both engines, and the optional executable built with Oracle GraalVM. gruszka and nano-lean were measured again on all eight corpora with their arena run lines and 8 threads, in the same two windows as the executable's rows. The tree was regenerated by \src{bench/track/benchmarks.py} and has every row with its window; the table of the root README was regenerated from the same rows. What follows is the summary.}

